summary: "We examine measurement error arising from the use of large language models (LLMs) in domain-specific metadata-extraction tasks. Using studies that employ weather as an instrumental variable as a test case, we compare extraction performance across four model families and three prompting approaches. We identify common LLM failure modes in literature-review workflows and characterize tradeoffs among extraction approaches."
